What are Integrated In-Rack CDUs?
Integrated In-Rack Coolant Distribution Units (CDUs) are specialized components designed for liquid cooling systems in data centers. These units efficiently distribute coolant or water through server racks, maintaining optimal temperature and flow rates while preventing system contamination. CDUs integrate seamlessly with pumps, heat exchangers, and control units to enhance cooling performance in high-density computing environments.
While liquid-to-air CDUs currently dominate due to easier installation, liquid-to-liquid variants are gaining traction because of their superior cooling capabilities. Key players like Vertiv and Schneider Electric are innovating to address the growing need for scalable cooling solutions in hyperscale data centers.
